  "data": {
    "body": "Consider the linear transformation $T: \\mathbb{R}^{3} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^{3}$ given by\n\n\n\n\\[\nT\\left(\\left[\\begin{array}{l}\n1 \\\\\n0 \\\\\n0\n\\end{array}\\right]\\right)=\\left[\\begin{array}{l}\na \\\\\n1 \\\\\n2\n\\end{array}\\right], \\quad T\\left(\\left[\\begin{array}{l}\n0 \\\\\n1 \\\\\n0\n\\end{array}\\right]\\right)=\\left[\\begin{array}{r}\n-1 \\\\\n3 \\\\\n1\n\\end{array}\\right], \\quad T\\left(\\left[\\begin{array}{l}\n0 \\\\\n0 \\\\\n1\n\\end{array}\\right]\\right)=\\left[\\begin{array}{l}\n4 \\\\\na \\\\\n4\n\\end{array}\\right],\n\\]\n\nwhere $a$ is a real number. Which of the following statements are/is TRUE?\n\n(i) The linear transformation $T$ is one-to-one for every real value of $a$.\n\n(ii) The linear transformation is not onto for $a=2$.\n\n(iii) The standard matrix for the linear transformation $T$ (relative to the standard basis on $\\mathbb{R}^{3}$ ) has rank $3$ for all real numbers $a \\neq 2,8$.",
    "solution": [
      3
    ],
